1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,290
The naïve generator predicts each Jewel mark from global text and local coordinates.

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:09,446
It can learn marginal colors, covariance frequencies, and density.

3
00:00:09,446 --> 00:00:12,217
What it does not own is a persistent object.

4
00:00:12,217 --> 00:00:23,300
Independent local choices are statistically plausible but mutually inconsistent: one region votes for fur, another for metal, and successive time slabs disagree about identity.

5
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:28,779
The result is structured texture rather than a recognizable actor performing an action.

6
00:00:29,479 --> 00:00:45,264
Addressing a sixteen-by-sixteen-by-eight spacetime grid and predicting one of one-thousand-and-twenty-four local block phrases lowers direct token negative log likelihood to five-point-one-six-eight, fifteen-point-six percent better than the global posterior.

7
00:00:45,264 --> 00:00:47,641
Yet qualitative renders remain texture.

8
00:00:47,641 --> 00:00:51,359
That experiment is vital because it separates two hypotheses.

9
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:53,370
Local statistical modeling works.

10
00:00:53,370 --> 00:01:00,074
Recognizable composition still fails because no variable binds those local phrases into one object trajectory.

11
00:01:00,774 --> 00:01:06,333
The next oracle chooses one complete training-owned program for the entire spacetime window.

12
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:09,112
Nothing about the physical vocabulary changes.

13
00:01:09,112 --> 00:01:17,934
The same continuous centroids and one-thousand-and-twenty-four-way active tokens suddenly render recognizable ballerina, dog, and welder examples.

14
00:01:17,934 --> 00:01:21,619
This is retrieval-only and therefore not the final generator.

15
00:01:21,619 --> 00:01:26,755
But causally, it identifies persistent cross-block ownership as the missing variable.

16
00:01:27,455 --> 00:01:31,709
A complete-source owner could be dismissed as nearest-neighbor playback.

17
00:01:31,709 --> 00:01:35,431
So the next experiment composes two distinct training programs.

18
00:01:35,431 --> 00:01:41,339
A moving foreground tube selects material from one donor; everything outside is supplied by another.

19
00:01:41,339 --> 00:01:48,369
Wrong-object controls deliberately take the foreground donor from a different semantic scene while preserving the path.

20
00:01:48,369 --> 00:01:49,906
The visible subject swaps.

21
00:01:49,906 --> 00:01:54,927
The field is therefore a new composition, and the tube has causal semantic ownership.

22
00:01:55,627 --> 00:02:04,267
For each addressed block, the realizer compares the scene's mean normalized descriptor with the mean of all other scenes and squares the difference.

23
00:02:04,267 --> 00:02:07,361
A centered spatial prior suppresses unstable borders.

24
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:14,074
Summing saliency over u and v yields one center per time slab, then a one-two-one temporal filter smooths the path.

25
00:02:14,074 --> 00:02:21,371
The path therefore follows where a class differs from alternatives, not where two arbitrary source fields happen to disagree.

26
00:02:22,071 --> 00:02:29,063
A single geometric radius can select unequal totals because different valid fields have different local densities.

27
00:02:29,063 --> 00:02:36,361
Instead, Gate two-b-zero sorts foreground Jewels by increasing squared tube distance and takes the closest half-budget.

28
00:02:36,361 --> 00:02:41,759
It sorts background Jewels in the opposite direction and takes the farthest half-budget.

29
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:50,530
Top-k selection makes the emitted count exact, forces fifty-fifty ownership, and requires no adjustment duplicates or target-derived threshold.

30
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:54,426
Every intended prompt is rendered under three seeds.

31
00:02:54,426 --> 00:03:02,970
Under the same declared seed, a cyclic-shuffled prompt compiles the next semantic scene, while a null prompt derives scene from seed alone.

32
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:10,223
Correct programs must beat those generated controls, not merely score against alternative text on an unchanged render.

33
00:03:10,223 --> 00:03:17,599
This distinction matters: it tests whether changing text causes the generated field to change in the intended direction.
